      "title": "To be fragile together",
      "description": "Tasos Sagris describes what care offers: no solution, no power, no profit, no mechanically calculated outcome. It is participation in the vulnerability of the other, a way to share our fragility and to be fragile together. In an era that demands strong personalities and self-sufficient professionals, admitting that someone needs an embrace, a kind word or a glass of understanding reads as scandalous. The speaker calls that admission resistance, a social and political act, and says compassion is a verb. From the workshop \"The Revolt of Care: Anarchist Mutual Aid in the 21st Century\" at the 2026 International Workshops. A Radical Guide is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit that builds movement infrastructu",
